  "context": "Compiled by Friedrich Engels from Marx's uncompleted manuscripts after his death, Volume 2 focuses on capital in motion: how capital transitions between money-capital, productive-capital, and commodity-capital, and how total social reproduction is maintained across production departments.",
  "relatesToToday": "Explains modern supply chain bottlenecks, inventory crises, and Amazon fulfillment centers. When goods sit in warehouses or container ships during global supply disruptions, capital is trapped and money stops circulating, causing sudden price surges and corporate panic.",
  "keyTakeaways": [
    "Capital is not a static object but a continuous cycle passing through money, productive, and commodity forms.",
    "Turnover time (production time plus circulation time) affects the rate and mass of annual profit.",
    "Social reproduction requires proportionality between Department I (means of production) and Department II (means of consumption)."
  ],
